# CRS (`crs`)

User invokes `crs` or `crs <modifier>`. **Check → report → suggest. No implementation.**

## Modifiers (suffix after `crs`)

- *(none)* — full audit: ✅/🟢/⚠️/❌ bullets, then 💡 when gaps exist (≤5 bullets total)
- `🟢−` — **gaps only:** omit all ✅ and 🟢 lines; optional one-line `🟢 N skipped`; then ⚠️/❌ and 💡
- `📋` — report only, no 💡 (≤5)
- `💡` — suggest only; assumes prior context (≤5); every bullet is 💡
- `🔍` — deep audit (≤8); still no implementation

## Response format (required)

- No preamble, tables, recap, or engagement closer.
- **Every bullet begins with exactly one status emoji:** ✅ done · 🟢 OK · ⚠️ partial/drift · ❌ missing/wrong · 💡 suggest
- Default `crs`: mix ✅/🟢/⚠️/❌ as needed; add ≥1 💡 bullet when anything is ⚠️ or ❌; omit 💡 if all ✅/🟢
- `🟢−`: only ⚠️, ❌, and 💡 bullets (never ✅ or 🟢 as line items)
- `💡`: every bullet starts with 💡

## Example (`crs 🟢−`)

- ❌ No scoped `database-ops.mdc` for PK/`bubble_id` rules
- 💡 Add `database-ops.mdc` globs for `contracts/schema.dbml` and future `supabase/**`
